---
permalink: /admin/messages/
title: "Messages | Admin"
bodyScripts:
  - src: "/scripts/admin-messages.js"
    type: "module"
  - src: "/scripts/contact-widget.js"
    type: "module"
---
<section class="app-page">
  {# Wider than the other reading pages: this one is a list to scan, not prose to read. The
     message bodies are constrained individually when they open. #}
  {% include "chrome/admin-sections.njk" %}

  <div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-x-4 gap-y-1 mb-2">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-brand-text">Messages</h1>
    <p id="messageCount" class="text-sm text-brand-muted"></p>
  </div>
  <p class="text-brand-muted mb-6 max-w-prose">
    Sent through the contact form, on either site. Replying happens in your email.
  </p>

  <div id="status" role="status" aria-live="polite" class="mb-4 text-sm"></div>

  {# --- controls ---------------------------------------------------------
     Filter and page size, both reflected in the URL so a view can be linked, bookmarked and
     returned to with the back button.

     There is no sort control, deliberately. The API returns newest first and pages by a cursor,
     so a control here could only reorder the page already fetched - which would look like
     sorting the inbox and would not be. Oldest-first would need the server to order the other
     way and hand back a cursor for it. #}
  <div class="flex flex-wrap items-end justify-between gap-4 mb-4">
    <div role="group" aria-label="Filter" class="inline-flex rounded-lg border border-brand-muted/20 p-1">
      <button type="button" id="filterAll" class="seg" aria-pressed="true">All</button>
      <button type="button" id="filterUnread" class="seg" aria-pressed="false">Unread</button>
    </div>

    <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
      <label for="pageSize" class="text-sm text-brand-muted">Per page</label>
      <select id="pageSize" class="field w-auto py-1.5 text-sm">
        <option value="25">25</option>
        <option value="50">50</option>
        <option value="100">100</option>
      </select>
    </div>
  </div>

  {# One row per message, each a native disclosure. The list holds one page and is replaced
     rather than appended to, so the page does not grow as the inbox does. #}
  <div id="messages">
    <p class="text-sm text-brand-muted">Loading messages…</p>
  </div>

  <nav aria-label="Pages" class="mt-6 flex items-center justify-between gap-4">
    <button type="button" id="newer" class="btn-secondary text-sm" disabled>Newer</button>
    <p id="pageWhere" class="text-sm text-brand-muted tabular-nums"></p>
    <button type="button" id="older" class="btn-secondary text-sm" disabled>Older</button>
  </nav>

</section>
